     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear INLA developers<div><br><div>It is clear that INLA can deal with space time model with separable variance covariance matrix. </div><div>E.g. In Cameletti&#39;s case, they use an additive form to capture the real spatiotemporal effects.<br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Tav5VYC_icc/Ww2EPDx3hdI/AAAAAAAAETU/jNlFp5Yz4xgeG6vZQyWao1Sk7tml_y5_ACLcBGAs/s1600/1.gif\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Tav5VYC_icc/Ww2EPDx3hdI/AAAAAAAAETU/jNlFp5Yz4xgeG6vZQyWao1Sk7tml_y5_ACLcBGAs/s1600/1.gif&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792443273037000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1L_iPTkSjMDrzg5uhSaslh\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Tav5VYC_icc/Ww2EPDx3hdI/AAAAAAAAETU/jNlFp5Yz4xgeG6vZQyWao1Sk7tml_y5_ACLcBGAs/s1600/1.gif\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Sn6AnWInF7I/Ww2EWH2HvHI/AAAAAAAAETY/xUbnNid5B1g2R7v_yjm3lD7L_rpRZpt4wCLcBGAs/s1600/2.gif\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Sn6AnWInF7I/Ww2EWH2HvHI/AAAAAAAAETY/xUbnNid5B1g2R7v_yjm3lD7L_rpRZpt4wCLcBGAs/s1600/2.gif&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792443273037000&amp;usg=AOvVaw130G0CBFsO01qweH24IodH\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Sn6AnWInF7I/Ww2EWH2HvHI/AAAAAAAAETY/xUbnNid5B1g2R7v_yjm3lD7L_rpRZpt4wCLcBGAs/s1600/2.gif\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vIh-9V0WBXc/Ww2EYuTpFNI/AAAAAAAAETc/d5R2Sxs6rkUK5qkIYdyOpEKFSEN5ODMoQCLcBGAs/s1600/4.gif\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vIh-9V0WBXc/Ww2EYuTpFNI/AAAAAAAAETc/d5R2Sxs6rkUK5qkIYdyOpEKFSEN5ODMoQCLcBGAs/s1600/4.gif&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792443273037000&amp;usg=AOvVaw10ydKlzZwIMMMmWl0li73d\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-vIh-9V0WBXc/Ww2EYuTpFNI/AAAAAAAAETc/d5R2Sxs6rkUK5qkIYdyOpEKFSEN5ODMoQCLcBGAs/s1600/4.gif\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><div>Indeed, I would like to know if INLA can deal with the following model, with a product formed variance covariance matrix?</div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Y2i4zfGMcII/Ww2GeZ7ZmaI/AAAAAAAAETw/eFSrYsGoj6I8T_TQMkuZR1nvYS5cMRUXQCLcBGAs/s1600/CodeCogsEqn.gif\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Y2i4zfGMcII/Ww2GeZ7ZmaI/AAAAAAAAETw/eFSrYsGoj6I8T_TQMkuZR1nvYS5cMRUXQCLcBGAs/s1600/CodeCogsEqn.gif&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792443273037000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3VF7v5bzdZZ0HQdvVzb7eg\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Y2i4zfGMcII/Ww2GeZ7ZmaI/AAAAAAAAETw/eFSrYsGoj6I8T_TQMkuZR1nvYS5cMRUXQCLcBGAs/s1600/CodeCogsEqn.gif\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div>Example cases exist? <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div>LING</div></div></div>"
